A||||8||Mach10||Quickie: Alternator problems||||8||
Z||000000||Mach10||07-12-2001||02:34 AM||||After changing my waterpump without a hitch (well, not counting my poor hands), my belt is screaming like a banshee. <BR>However hard I try, I can't find a damn place to lever on the alternator to get some tension. How the HELL do I tighten this damn thing?!?||||reg||8
Z||000001||fierospeeder||07-12-2001||03:22 AM||||what engine?||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSoul||07-12-2001||06:48 AM||||  They make a nice turnbuckle type thing to push the pulleys apart if you can find one. Available through JC Whitney for sure.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||07-12-2001||09:56 AM||||may just do it for a short time if any dripped on pullies or belt during the change<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||07-12-2001||11:13 AM||||Sorry, v6. I know that the antifreese did splash on it, so I was thinking so too, but I took it out for a pretty long drive (~50km) and it did it more or less constant the whole way. Oh well, I'll try again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>||||reg||8
Z||000005||k2m4||07-12-2001||11:19 AM||||On my 2m4 i use a simple old Tire iron (the one that looks like a screw driver on the opposite end of the socket) its long enough and gives you enough leverage to hold and tighten the alternater  tensioner bolt. or just Go to your local hardware automotive store and get a pry bar for 5 bucks. Have fun!<BR>kerm<BR>86 2M4<BR>86 1/2 GT  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||07-12-2001||01:48 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> Mach10's Approved Alternator Tightening Procedure  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>Tools:<BR>-Extensive vocabulary<BR>-Bar from hydraulic jack<BR>-several pieces of Cedar shingling<P>Jam the bar beside the exhaust manifold, and between the block and alternator. Wedge the chunks of wood 'twixt the block and your bar. Have a friend haul on the bar while you shimmy underneath and tighten the adjusting bolt. Swear profusely when your buddy slips, and the pieces of wood rain on your face, repeat.||||reg||14
Z||000007||thomas_l||07-12-2001||02:16 PM||||If you have a big pair of channel-lock pliers, you can put one jaw on the adjust bracket and the other against the back of the bolt (on the alternator). Squeeze the handles to the desired belt tightness and lock it down.<P>Have fun!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000008||Mach10||07-12-2001||03:41 PM||||MOTHER-#@!# !@#$!#$ !#$%@#$%@#<BR>Why the HELL didn't I think of that?!?!???<BR>*SMACK*<BR>*SMACK*<BR>*SMACK*||||reg||8
